positive integers as required. No hypotheses are added or dropped, domains are real, and the quantifier structure over x is correct.", "differences": ["The candidate hardcodes the five integers rather than universally quantifying over any representation, so it must prove the exact closed form rather than deduce the sum from a given representation (a common but different encoding); the final sum assertion becomes a trivial arithmetic identity."], "equivalent": true, "confidence": 0.72}}, "status": "UNDECIDED", "reason": "judges disagreed (gpt_5_6_sol=no 0.98, claude_opus_5=yes 0.72)"}
