{"index": 464, "problem": "Suppose three real polynomials in two variables have total degrees two, three, and four respectively, that the discriminant of the quadratic they form in a third variable (with the degree-two one as leading coefficient, the degree-three one as middle coefficient, and the degree-four one as constant term) is, at every real point, the negative of the square of the value of some fixed real polynomial in those two variables, and that this quadratic is never negative when all three variables run over the reals; prove that there are two real polynomials in the three variables whose squares sum, at every real point, to the value of that quadratic.", "candidate": "theorem quadratic_is_sum_of_two_squares (p₂ p₃ p₄ : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) ℝ) (hdeg₂ : MvPolynomial.totalDegree p₂ = 2) (hdeg₃ : MvPolynomial.totalDegree p₃ = 3) (hdeg₄ : MvPolynomial.totalDegree p₄ = 4) (hdisc : ∃ q : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) ℝ, ∀ x y : ℝ, (MvPolynomial.eval ![x, y] p₃) ^ 2 - 4 * MvPolynomial.eval ![x, y] p₂ * MvPolynomial.eval ![x, y] p₄ = -((MvPolynomial.eval ![x, y] q) ^ 2)) (hnonneg : ∀ x y z : ℝ, 0 ≤ MvPolynomial.eval ![x, y] p₂ * z ^ 2 + MvPolynomial.eval ![x, y] p₃ * z + MvPolynomial.eval ![x, y] p₄) : ∃ A B : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℝ, ∀ x y z : ℝ, (MvPolynomial.eval ![x, y, z] A) ^ 2 + (MvPolynomial.eval ![x, y, z] B) ^ 2 = MvPolynomial.eval ![x, y] p₂ * z ^ 2 + MvPolynomial.eval ![x, y] p₃ * z + MvPolynomial.eval ![x, y] p₄ := by sorry", "reference": "theorem omni_theorem_116 (A B C : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) ℝ) (hA : A.totalDegree = 2) (hB : B.totalDegree = 3) (hC : C.totalDegree = 4) (R : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) ℝ) (hR : ∀ x y : ℝ, (eval (fun n => if n = 0 then x else y) B) ^ 2 - 4 * (eval (fun n => if n = 0 then x else y) A) * (eval (fun n => if n = 0 then x else y) C) = -(eval (fun n => if n = 0 then x else y) R) ^ 2) (hA' : ∀ x y z : ℝ, (eval (fun n => if n = 0 then x else y) A) * z ^ 2 + (eval (fun n => if n = 0 then x else y) B) * z + (eval (fun n => if n = 0 then x el