S (3+2\\u221a2), i.e. 3+2\\u221a2 \\u2208 S and it is an upper bound of S. Since S is downward closed, this is equivalent to the reference's iff formulation (m \\u2208 S \\u2194 m \\u2264 3+2\\u221a2). Domains: positive naturals vs positive integers \\u2014 mathematically the same set of quadruples. Constraints a+b=c+d, 2ab=cd, b \\u2264 a match (a \\u2265 b). Conclusion asserts the answer 3+2\\u221a2, matching. Coercions are to \\u211d so the ratio is a real division, as intended.", "differences": [], "equivalent": true, "confidence": 0.9}}, "status": "EQUIVALENT", "reason": "gpt_5_6_sol=yes 1.00, claude_opus_5=yes 0.90"}
